-- title:
--   Compatibility of w_q with the degeneracy inclusion of j-expansion fields
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$, $q$, $\ell$ with $N_0$ and $\ell$ nonzero and $q$ prime (as a `Fact`), and assume $q \nmid N_0\ell$. Here, for a nonzero level $N$, `modularFunctionFieldFull N` denotes the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of series $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ \mathrm{jq}$ for nonzero divisors $d \mid N$, and `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N ℓ` is a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * ℓ)` chosen, when one exists, so as to satisfy `IsAtkinLehnerAutFull N ℓ`, i.e. to interchange $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ \mathrm{jq}$ and $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ (d\ell)\ \mathrm{jq}$ for every nonzero $d \mid N$ (and to be the identity otherwise). Given $f$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)` and $f'$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * ℓ * q)` whose underlying Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ coincide, the assertion is that the Laurent series underlying `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull (N₀ * ℓ) q f'` equals the Laurent series underlying `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N₀ q f`. Thus the Atkin–Lehner automorphism at level $N_0\ell q$ restricts, on the subfield of level $N_0 q$, to the one at level $N_0 q$.
--
--   This is the $w_q$-equivariance of the first degeneracy map between the $j$-expansion function fields of levels $N_0\ell q$ and $N_0 q$, stated in the form 'elements with equal $q$-expansions have $w_q$-images with equal $q$-expansions'. It is used in the construction of the degeneracy/Atkin–Lehner package for the modular curves, in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.w_hom_comp_eq_comp_w_hom_of_pinned`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.w_hom_comp_eq_comp_w_hom_of_pinned) and in a prolongation statement about integral points of places.
